<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45543" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὕω</span></b> , aor. 1
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὗσα</span> (v. infr.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>singe</i>, esp. of singeing off the bristles of
			swine before they are cooked, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὗσέ τε μίστυλλέν τε καὶ ἀμφ᾽
					ὀβελοῖσιν ἔπειρεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					14.75
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				426
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.300
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύες εὑόμενοι τανύοντο διὰ φλογός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.468
				</span></i>
			; so of the Cyclops, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάντα δέ οἱ βλέφαρ᾽ ἀμφὶ καὶ ὀφρύας
					εὗσεν ἀϋτμή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					9.389
				</span></i>
			: metaph., of a shrewish wife, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνδρα . . εὕει ἄτερ δαλοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					705
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὔει</span> codd. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
			</span></i>). (Sts. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔω</span> in codd.,
				v.l.
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.468
			</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				401.24
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				2.300
			</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				398.34
			</span></i>), Hes.l.c.: but 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφ-εύω, ἐφεύω</span>
			; cf. Lat. <i>uro</i> fr.
		*<i>eus-ō.</i>)</div>
